  "evidence": [
    "Pinned Net::get630A00 returns NetGetScratch9BC4BC iff queue result word is nonzero. Mapped callers52 sites in18 NetDaemon functions pass EAX bits to existing process_message(char*) sink. Pointer semantics are proved; stripped original does not prove declared C++ return type.",
    "Preserve absent DirectPlay/key-output rejection, lack of length-output null guard/capacity clamp, empty queue untouched outputs, consumed zero-result nodes that still copy/write outputs, nonzero-result null-payload nodes that expose stale shared scratch, and shared overwrite lifetime. NetFifo get/peek remain integer result methods, not pointer producers.",
    "Net sibling sub_630A40/630980/6309C0 API changes are outside this bounded intent; keep their bodies/prototypes unchanged. All Net/NetDaemon identities are measurement scope due header/inlining impact. Coordinator verifies emitted getter symbol and publishes through native writer; workers never edit original markers or grant/demote claims."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover the live Net::get shared packet pointer API and its complete NetDaemon consumers, preserving FIFO integer result semantics, queue side effects, scratch lifetime and original failure behavior. No sibling-wrapper or bug-fix expansion.",
